        <STYLE css="color:#808080;font-style:italic"> upon </STYLE> the <gr str="3220">sea</gr>: </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="6"> Which by his <gr str="3581">strength </gr>setteth <gr str="3559">fast </gr>the <gr str="2022">mountains</gr>; <STYLE css="color:#808080;font-style:italic"> being </STYLE>
        <gr str="247">girded </gr>with <gr str="1369">power</gr>: </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="7"> Which <gr str="7623">stilleth </gr>the <gr str="7588">noise </gr>of the <gr str="3220">seas</gr>, the <gr str="7588">noise </gr>of their <gr str="1530">waves</gr>, and the <gr str="1995">tumult </gr>of the <gr str="3816">people</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="8"> They also that <gr str="3427">dwell </gr>in the uttermost <gr str="7098">parts </gr>are <gr str="3372">afraid </gr>at thy <gr str="4480 226">tokens</gr>: thou makest the <gr str="4161">outgoings </gr>of the <gr str="1242">morning </gr>and <gr str="6153">evening </gr>to <gr str="7442">rejoice</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="9"> Thou <gr str="6485">visitest </gr>the <gr str="776">earth</gr>, and <gr str="7783">waterest </gr>it: thou <gr str="7227">greatly </gr>
