        <gr str="3559">provided </gr>for it. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="10"> Thou waterest the <gr str="8525">ridges </gr>thereof <gr str="7301">abundantly</gr>: thou <gr str="5181">settlest </gr>the <gr str="1417">furrows </gr>thereof: thou makest it <gr str="4127">soft </gr>with <gr str="7241">showers</gr>: thou <gr str="1288">blessest </gr>the <gr str="6780">springing </gr>thereof. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="11"> Thou <gr str="5849">crownest </gr>the <gr str="8141">year </gr>with thy <gr str="2896">goodness</gr>; and thy <gr str="4570">paths </gr>
        <gr str="7491">drop </gr>
        <gr str="1880">fatness</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="12"> They <gr str="7491">drop </gr>
        <STYLE css="color:#808080;font-style:italic"> upon </STYLE> the <gr str="4999">pastures </gr>of the <gr str="4057">wilderness</gr>: and the little <gr str="1389">hills </gr>
        <gr str="1524">rejoice </gr>on every <gr str="2296">side</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="13"> The <gr str="3733">pastures </gr>are <gr str="3847">clothed </gr>with <gr str="6629">flocks</gr>; the <gr str="6010">valleys </gr>also are covered <gr str="5848">over </gr>with <gr str="1250">corn</gr>; they shout for <gr str="7321">joy</gr>, they <gr str="637">also </gr>
        <gr str="7891">sing</gr>. </VERS>
